1
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,520
But Chief Ohara told us not
to lend Ryo-chan any money.

2
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,720
Wow, when I say I won't lend it,
I really won't.

3
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:24,020
I'm not asking you, I'm asking Reiko.

4
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:26,478
We're about to eat our lunch.

5
00:00:26,528 --> 00:00:28,200
You're in the way, so go away.

6
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,100
Here's your order.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:33,009
Please, Reiko, if 500 yen is no good,
300 yen is fine too.

8
00:00:33,059 --> 00:00:35,580
No, with 150 yen I can get a cup noodle...

9
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,300
If I spin three times and say "woof"...

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,280
Wow!

11
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,100
Kankichi

12
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,300
Lemon

13
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,020
What on earth are you doing?

14
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,520
I'm just doing a dog impression.

15
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:51,680
There's a pubic hair contest at the Hatsuyo next time,
you know.

16
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:53,160
Or rather, practice for it.

17
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:55,800
I've got about 150 yen on me.

18
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:57,740
That's fine, Lemon-chan.

19
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,040
I'll lend Ryo-chan his lunch money.

20
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,320
Honestly, Reiko, you're such a softie.

21
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,300
If you were watching,
you should've said so from the start.

22
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,040
Anyway, Lemon, what did you come here for?

23
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:15,200
Actually, I'm going to have a baby.

24
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,620
A baby is going to be born.

25
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:27,140
When you watch TV, turn the lights
on and sit back from the screen.

26
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:44,960
Anyone broke, come to me.
I've got no money either, but don't worry.

27
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:58,740
Look at that blue sky, those white clouds.
Things will work out somehow.

28
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:37,540
You understand, right?

29
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,520
I get it, I get it.

30
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:43,460
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

31
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,980
A baby's being born?

32
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,340
You don't mean...

33
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:12,260
What are you doing all of a sudden?

34
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:15,560
A kindergartener can't possibly have a baby.

35
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,260
Speaking of which,

36
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:20,180
So that means the baby came from...

37
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:24,980
No way.

38
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:28,020
Mato-chan, is your stomach okay?

39
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:31,380
I'm fine, it just hurts a little.

40
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:37,500
M-Mato-chan?

41
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,520
D-don't tell me...

42
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:42,660
What are you staring at?

43
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,720
No way.

44
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,660
Mato-chan's...

45
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,200
What are you talking about?

46
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:54,100
Well, if Mato got knocked up,
there's nothing to be done.

47
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,680
So when is the baby in her belly due?

48
00:03:56,680 --> 00:04:00,700
Why do I have to be the one having a baby?

49
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:05,020
Kankichi, are you alright?

50
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:07,480
Why are you here?

51
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:11,020
I came to tell Kankichi about the baby.

52
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:12,480
And then?

53
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:17,000
Didn't Mato-chan get pregnant?

54
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,420
I don't remember saying that.

55
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,340
But you were touching her belly.

56
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:23,273
That was...

57
00:04:23,323 --> 00:04:28,960
Mato-chan took on the challenge of eating 50 gyoza in 10 minutes for free,
and she finished them all.

58
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,580
Then who on earth is having the baby?

59
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:35,180
Our mom.

60
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:45,300
So that means you're getting a little brother or sister, Lemon.
That's great, isn't it? Good for you, Lemon.

61
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:52,960
Stop it, that's embarrassing.
I see, you'll be a big sister soon

62
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,260
Big sister.

63
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,520
Lemon's going to be a big sister.

64
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,660
Come on in.

65
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:12,060
Reiko, Nakagawa, welcome.

66
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,240
Good evening.

67
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,480
Sorry for barging in on you like this.

68
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,700
Not at all.

69
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,520
Barging in? No way, you're always welcome.

70
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:19,860
We're so glad you came.

71
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:23,700
Well, I had no idea
Lemon's mom was pregnant.

72
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:25,480
I didn't notice at all.

73
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,620
Not that it has anything
to do with Kankichi, though.

74
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:28,520
Mom.

75
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,980
This is just a trifling little gift, but

76
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:33,120
it's from us too.

77
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:33,660
Please, take it.

78
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:38,340
Kankichi's trifling gift is really trifling,
you know.

79
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:39,680
You shouldn't have.

80
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,680
If it's from you two,
we'll gladly accept it.

81
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,580
Thank you.

82
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:47,140
Ugh, it's so true it just makes me angrier.

83
00:05:48,940 --> 00:05:50,960
You're giving birth at home?

84
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,040
Mato and Lemon were born at home too.

85
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:57,020
Now that you mention it, when I was a kid,

86
00:05:57,020 --> 00:05:59,980
home births were the norm in the old downtown,
weren't they?

87
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:03,020
But do midwives even exist these days?

88
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,700
Sure, there are veteran ones,
though they're pretty old.

89
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,020
The midwife who delivered me is one of them.

90
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:09,720
Hey.

91
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,920
Since Grandma is 101 years old.

92
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,800
How old is this midwife, anyway?

93
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,220
Tome-san is 119.

94
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:19,620
An ambulance

95
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,820
Mato-chan says hi too, nice to meet you.

96
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:25,300
Tome-san delivered almost
everyone in the neighborhood.

97
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:29,600
104 years as a midwife,
over 10,000 babies delivered.

98
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:33,300
Come to think of it, I was born at home too.

99
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:37,060
What? Nakagawa, the rich one,
was born at home like me?

100
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:39,140
Somehow I feel a sense of kinship.

101
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:39,900
Is that so?

102
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:45,180
I believe 50 doctors and 100
midwives came to our house.

103
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,700
So many doctors wanted to come
that they had to hold a lottery.

104
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:52,780
It was even broadcast live on TV,
all across America.

105
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,220
Ahaha, I was so embarrassed.

106
00:06:55,220 --> 00:06:56,620
Figures, it's totally different.

107
00:06:57,280 --> 00:07:00,760
That little bit of kinship
I felt was my own mistake.

108
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:04,340
Have the names been decided yet?

109
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,760
Not yet.

110
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,280
Then I'll come up with some names for them.

111
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:12,660
Father "Yoroshiku"
(Nice to meet you), eldest son "Yuuutsu" (Gloomy).

112
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:15,480
Eldest daughter "Mato"
(Fire Brigade Banner), second daughter "Lemon."

113
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:18,360
So how about this one?

114
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:20,640
Gibo-bara.

115
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:23,060
Rose, that's a cute one.

116
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,720
I've got more where that came from.

117
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:28,560
A machine like that? Pretty?

118
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,720
Having so many hidden meanings doesn't make
"Tsuki" a good name!

119
00:07:32,820 --> 00:07:34,700
Why soy sauce?! Are you an idiot?!

120
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:36,900
You're just matching your brothers' names,
you know!

121
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:41,340
Fine. Since they're a sushi shop's kids,
how about names like these?

122
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,609
Saba, Tako, Maguro, Kisu,

123
00:07:44,659 --> 00:07:46,740
Shimāji, surume-ika?

124
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:49,420
Kaakichi! That's not a sushi shop's teacup!

125
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,920
Giboshi, surume-ika,
what kind of names are those?!

126
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:55,960
You lot are so noisy.
Then let's go with Gepard.

127
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:59,615
Rommel, Tiger, Leopard, Merkava,

128
00:07:59,665 --> 00:08:02,420
Challenger, what about Type 90?

129
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,295
Mm-hmm,

130
00:08:04,345 --> 00:08:07,540
Why are you naming the
grandchild after tanks!

131
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:08,460
Got it, got it!

132
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:12,800
Then how about Gibōshi,
Carl Gustaf, Mako, F, or Belladonna?

133
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:14,420
Those are names for people
from a useless country!

134
00:08:14,740 --> 00:08:17,140
Lemon-chan, what kind of name do you like?

135
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:21,260
I can't think of one yet.
I have to see its face first.

136
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:21,820
There!

137
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,220
I hope it's born healthy.

138
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,500
It'll be fine, Lemon.

139
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,380
Lemon, what's wrong?

140
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:46,700
Has it been born?

141
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,940
No. Where's Kankichi?

142
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,420
He's out on patrol.

143
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:55,160
He'll be back soon, so you can wait for him.

144
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:58,280
If he's not here, never mind. Well then.

145
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:09,340
There we are!
A big haul after such a long time.

146
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:18,900
Lemon, what are you
doing in a place like this?

147
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:20,104
Kankichi,

148
00:09:20,154 --> 00:09:23,380
how long are you going to keep patrolling?

149
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,961
Well, various things happened.

150
00:09:26,011 --> 00:09:27,940
Anyway, what's up?

151
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,140
Yeah.

152
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:32,960
Kankichi.

153
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:34,620
What?

154
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:38,440
But will she really be
able to become a big sister?

155
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,420
Actually...

156
00:09:50,360 --> 00:10:18,880

Translation>
I'm so, so... eh, cough
Oh, I'll go! Now let's talk with someone...

157
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:22,140
He cried because he peed.

158
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:24,600
Makoto, you can even tell that?

159
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:25,300
Well, yeah.

160
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:28,540
Oh my, Ma-kun, you're so clever.

161
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:30,960
Just like a big brother, after all.

162
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,960
Lemon doesn't seem like
she'll make a good big sister.

163
00:10:43,620 --> 00:10:45,500
So that's what you've been moping about?

164
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:50,020
Don't worry,
Lemon will make a great big sister.

165
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:50,700
You think so?

166
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:53,480
Of course. I guarantee it.

167
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:01,980
So that's what Lemon's been worrying about

168
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:05,980
This will be Lemon's
first younger family member.

169
00:11:05,980 --> 00:11:09,180
Lemon must have her own mix of hopes and anxieties,
don't you think?

170
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,400
To help her build some confidence,

171
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:17,200
maybe we should have Lemon help
out with the birth somehow too.

172
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,820
In what way?

173
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,360
Yeah, so basically,

174
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:26,240
Wait, Lemon's the one
who's going to fetch her?

175
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:30,260
It's a home birth,
so someone has to go get Tome-san.

176
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:32,460
To have her deliver the baby.

177
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:35,160
Tome-san?
Is she the one who came by the other day?

178
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:41,120
That's right. It's a really important job.

179
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,860
Got it! Lemon will do her best!

180
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:50,780
Happy Lemon's been given a job!

181
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:52,880
It's an important job, you know.

182
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,160
Kankichi,
you actually said something good for once.

183
00:11:57,460 --> 00:11:58,320
Right.

184
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,240
Hello?

185
00:12:07,420 --> 00:12:10,840
Lemon. So you took it on?

186
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:14,500
I think it'll be fine, but just in case,
there's always a chance something happens.

187
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:18,700
If that happens, you'll take
responsibility and look after it, right?

188
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:21,700
You worry too much. You'll go gray.

189
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,080
Unnecessary work.

190
00:12:23,420 --> 00:12:26,300
Yeah, got it, got it.
I'll back you up properly.

191
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:27,840
See ya.

192
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:35,160
This is the road on the right.

193
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:40,200
That's right. It helps to remember
distinctive buildings and things like that.

194
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:45,060
Traffic is heavy around here, so be careful.

195
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:45,960
Got it.

196
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:49,080
Turn into the alley beside this post office.

197
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,280
The second house is Tome-san's place.

198
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:54,100
I'll go check.

199
00:13:01,160 --> 00:13:02,000
Is this it?

200
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:02,500
Yeah.

201
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:17,360
Thank you.

202
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:25,260
Lemon, you're back.

203
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:27,980
A-are you still okay?

204
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:31,320
No contractions yet, I'm fine.

205
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:34,840
Thank goodness,
I thought we wouldn't make it in time.

206
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,200
Even if today is the due date,

207
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:40,620
Ah

208
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,740
Ugh... haa...

209
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,500
W-this is terrible!

210
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:01,020
What? Her labor has started?

211
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,060
Whoa!

212
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:03,940
So, where's Lemon?

213
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:07,620
Right, I see, got it. Leave the rest to me!

214
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,160
Did I catch up?

215
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,540
Oh no, what do I do?

216
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:33,560
Well, if I take the left road and turn right,
it should be fine, right?

217
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:41,600
Ugh, of all times,
a road closure in an emergency like this!

218
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,480
Seriously,
Tokyo has way too much road construction.

219
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,780
Turn right here.

220
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:50,780
Good, that's it, Lemon.

221
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:52,980
Construction here too?

222
00:14:53,740 --> 00:14:54,600
Here too.

223
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,240
Here too?

224
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,660
I think it's this road, probably.

225
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,140
Lemon, that's wrong!

226
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,980
You're supposed to turn left at
the next traffic light, though.

227
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:15,100
Damn it!

228
00:15:15,860 --> 00:15:17,620
Lemon, please notice!

229
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:23,000
Something's off here.

230
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:26,500
There should be a post
office by now, though.

231
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:32,720
Listen, you're getting farther
and farther from Tome-san's house!

232
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:34,620
If I don't tell her quickly...

233
00:15:35,160 --> 00:15:38,540
Listen, Kankichi,
even on patrol you must never get caught!

234
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:41,700
Seeing it through to the end on
your own is what matters most, so.

235
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:42,680
Damn.

236
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:48,360
Alright, I can make it!

237
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:54,660
Damn, I've completely taken the wrong road.

238
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:55,920
What should I do?

239
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,560
You seem to be in trouble, don't you?

240
00:15:58,560 --> 00:16:03,180
How did you know?

241
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:05,960
I'm a very accurate
fortune-teller at the station.

242
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:08,540
I can tell everything just
by looking at your face.

243
00:16:08,540 --> 00:16:12,980
A station fortune-teller is like
the ones in period dramas, right?

244
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:16,800
In short,
it's a job where you help people in trouble.

245
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:17,720
Perfect timing.

246
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,400
But I'm really in trouble right now.

247
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:23,720
How do I get to Tome-san's place?

248
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,360
For Mom's sake, Tome-san...

249
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:27,924
Onlookers,

250
00:16:27,974 --> 00:16:32,200
for this earnest young lady, I'll read
your fortune for free, so believe me!

251
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,237
Honjara, honjara,

252
00:16:35,287 --> 00:16:37,640
Hoi, hoi, there it is!

253
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:42,420
go back the way you came,
turn left at the first traffic light,

254
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,600
go about 50 meters,
and you'll reach a dead end.

255
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,740
On your left, there's a post office.

256
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:49,460
Once you find the post office,
the rest is easy.

257
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:51,480
Thank you, fortune-teller.

258
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:58,420
Well, Officer, is that all?

259
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,840
Thanks, that really helped.

260
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:12,780
We've come far enough now, should be fine.

261
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:23,180
That's odd, it's been five minutes already.

262
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:26,180
Tome-san's not home.

263
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,620
There's a home birth over in Nezu, you see.

264
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:31,040
She's been at that house since last night,
you know.

265
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:33,720
Didn't a girl come by a little while ago?

266
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,460
I wrote down that house's
address in Nezu for her, and...

267
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:39,580
she said she'd go pick her up and ran off.

268
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:39,740
Well?

269
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:43,400
Damn! Old man, tell me that address too!

270
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:48,700
Dammit.

271
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:00,820
Did she leave it at home?

272
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:03,748
Damn, which way is it? This way? No,

273
00:18:03,798 --> 00:18:05,660
Could it be this way?

274
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:07,300
This way!

275
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:11,980
Where is Lemon right now?

276
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:13,840
It's just a Gepard

277
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:16,960
Lemon's lost? What is she doing?

278
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:18,920
What about Tome-san?

279
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:21,800
What? She's gone to another
pregnant woman's place?

280
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,660
W-what do we do?

281
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,240
It's labor, hurry up!

282
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:28,840
Yes.

283
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:37,380
Turn right at the second traffic light.
The third house is the Kuriharas'.

284
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:37,960
Thank you.

285
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:38,760
Don't mention it.

286
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:50,960
Yes, she left just a moment ago.

287
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:53,000
So, the kindergarten girl

288
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,600
didn't come by asking for Tome-san?

289
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,720
No, Tome-san went home alone.

290
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:00,120
Damn, did I take the wrong road?

291
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,980
If the girl happens to
come by in the meantime,

292
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:04,340
please ask her to call the house.

293
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:04,960
Hah.

294
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:06,800
Hey, Lemon!

295
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:08,580
Where are you?

296
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:11,060
Over here!

297
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:13,940
If you can hear me, answer!

298
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:16,980
Excuse me...

299
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,180
I'd like to ask you for directions...

300
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:22,640
I-it'd be better to ask at the police box...

301
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,680
You're a police officer, aren't you?

302
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:25,900
Yeah, that's right.

303
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,960
So, where are you trying to go?

304
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,500
Well, that's the thing...

305
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:34,140
Is the midwife not here yet?

306
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,080
They say it's about to fill up!

307
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,380
There's no choice.

308
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:44,120
I'll deliver the baby.

309
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,260
Are you all right?

310
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,020
We've got no choice but to do it

311
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:50,720
Granny.

312
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:53,620
I brought her!

313
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:56,200
Sorry I'm late.

314
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:57,780
Please get started right away.

315
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,920
This way, this way!

316
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:05,880
You look well.
I'm sure a good baby is going to be born.

317
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:07,980
There, everything's all right now.

318
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,900
It's okay, breathe out slowly.

319
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:15,700
Thank you for bringing her, dear.
There's nothing to worry about now.

320
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:22,700
Well, let's leave it to Tome-san
and make ourselves scarce.

321
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:36,880
The baby's been born safely?

322
00:20:37,560 --> 00:20:39,380
That cry sounds healthy.

323
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:47,900
Come here, Lemon.

324
00:20:56,620 --> 00:20:57,720
It's your little sister.

325
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:09,840
She's so small and cute.

326
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:13,820
She was waiting in my belly
until you got back, Lemon.

327
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:18,580
So she was waiting for you.

328
00:21:35,180 --> 00:21:37,480
Lemon's really dependable.

329
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:39,820
Is that so.

330
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:44,000
She came all the way to fetch Tome-san on her own,
you know.

331
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,100
She really did a great job.

332
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:50,260
Lemon, Tome-san praised you!

333
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:53,000
Since today you're a big sister now.

334
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,980
Suddenly you look so grown-up.

335
00:21:58,220 --> 00:22:00,040
Looks like you've gained some confidence.

336
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:07,520
Mikan, what a cute name.

337
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:11,200
From among the few names I'd thought up,

338
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:13,280
Lemon was the one who chose it for us.

339
00:22:58,260 --> 00:23:00,000
Lemon, let me hold her too.

340
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:02,620
What is it?

341
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:04,900
Here, leave her to me.

342
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:07,100
Why?

343
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:11,160
Well, hand her over to me.

344
00:23:13,860 --> 00:23:15,100
So her name's Mikan

345
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:20,560
Aaaahhh!

346
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:24,340
Ryo-chan, you're amazing!

347
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:28,560
Haha, Mikan has good taste in men.

348
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,060
Here, Lemon.

349
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:30,600
Yeah.

350
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:32,140
Kakishii.

351
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:37,540
Not just Tome-san and Lemon, you're fooling Mikan too?
Unforgivable!

352
00:23:38,040 --> 00:23:40,578
Eeeeh, to a baby who was just born,

353
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:42,760
what do you mean
"fooling"? Don't be ridiculous!

354
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,800
Hey, listen up!

355
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,460
Stop it, hey!

356
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:47,840
Enough already!

357
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:50,460
What is this? Stop it!

358
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:51,880
Hey, hey!

359
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:52,860
Hey, hey!

360
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:55,400
Hey, hey!

361
00:23:58,700 --> 00:24:00,580
She's really adorable, isn't she?

362
00:24:14,800 --> 00:24:18,700
Na na na na, na na na na

363
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:24,180
for those who gamble foolishly on looks

364
00:24:24,180 --> 00:24:27,380
I probably don't want to become one

365
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:31,960
if you're dawdling at the street corner

366
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:34,300
the moon has run away

367
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:37,840
because now isn't everything

368
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:42,520
don't get too worked up about it

369
00:24:42,520 --> 00:24:46,260
even if you lie a little and cheat a little

370
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:50,420
sometimes while helping someone

371
00:24:50,420 --> 00:24:52,440
Baby, do you know me?

372
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:56,760
a nice spirit facing toward tomorrow

373
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:01,780
don't rot away, just do what needs doing

374
00:25:01,780 --> 00:25:04,260
a cute spirit

375
00:25:04,260 --> 00:25:07,640
what's hard to understand is

376
00:25:08,780 --> 00:25:11,420
it's because you want to show off

377
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:17,220
isn't it better than
just changing your looks?

378
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:24,820
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

379
00:25:29,100 --> 00:25:32,020
Any Japanese person should
eat watermelon in summer, right?

380
00:25:32,020 --> 00:25:34,440
I eat nothing but watermelon
for all three meals!

381
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:36,460
What? Don't lie?

382
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:37,520
Alright, fine.

383
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:39,800
I'll live on nothing
but watermelon for a week.

384
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:42,240
But if I pull it off, it's a million yen!

385
00:25:42,520 --> 00:25:46,180
Next time: the man who finishes
300 watermelons in one week!

386
00:25:46,180 --> 00:25:47,620
Look forward to it.

387
00:25:48,500 --> 00:25:50,820
Over there is Kameari,

388
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:54,600
well, surely it's Kameari,

389
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:59,180
everyone, come on over to our town.

390
00:26:00,260 --> 00:26:00,780
Thank you.

